From 04646b857e0f1cfe1660d8641399bae807abb2a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhang Tingan <ZhangTingan@uniontech.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse Wayland shm buffers only while their device pixel ratio
 matches

QWaylandShmBackingStore::getBuffer() decided whether a pooled buffer
could be reused from its pixel size alone. A buffer sets its device
pixel ratio once, in its constructor, and nothing updates it afterwards,
so a buffer created for an earlier scale could be handed out again and
every frame painted into it was then drawn at the wrong size: part of
the surface was left with the previous content, or the content was
clipped.

The pixel size cannot stand in for the ratio. The requested size is
(logical size + margins) * scale, and a surface whose physical size is
pinned requests the same pixel size at every scale, so the scale cancels
out of the size and the reuse test has nothing left to compare.

Prune buffers whose ratio no longer matches the window scale, the same
way the pool already prunes on a mismatching size. Pruning, rather than
skipping such buffers in the selection loop, is required:
recreateBackBufferIfNeeded() blocks until getBuffer() returns a buffer,
so a pool full of skipped buffers would make getBuffer() return nullptr
and wait for a release event from buffers that are all idle and will
never produce one.

The existing QWaylandShmBuffer::scale() accessor is not used for the
comparison, because it returns int(devicePixelRatio()) and truncates
fractional scales.

